From: isoriano1968 <81116077+isoriano1968@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] 18700 applesmc: fans with "flt " keys (MacBook Pro 2016-2017)

Newer SMCs keep the fan keys (F<n>Ac, Mn, Mx, Tg) as "flt " (IEEE single
in rpm, little endian, 4 bytes) instead of fpe2.  The driver now accepts
both: it keeps fan values as rpm * 4 and converts at the SMC with integer
arithmetic; writes must use the key's own type and length.  smcfan reads
and writes either type.  APPLESMC_IOC_FANMIN still answers in fpe2.
---
